  "created": "2026-03-11T03:56:24.610Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The tos should not allow worlds to strip avatars of their features. Toggles, animations, shaders, meshes, gestures, contacts, rigs, constraints, physbones, colliders, textures, particle emitters, or gimmicks should not be allowed to be targeted by world creators.\n\n A recent example of this is in the Fish! world, where the creators have removed moderator's ability to promptly deal with problem users or do their job via disabling avatar colliders and seats. These basic components previously allowed moderators to quickly find problem users and warn/kick/ban them from a group. Now, problem users can hide in large worlds and have free rein to do whatever they want without a moderator being able to see them or get to them in a timely manner.\n\nAllowing worlds to strip basic features and components off of avatars can lead to avatar creators being blamed for the avatars lack of functionality. It can also lead to targeted harassment towards certain features such as certain skin tones (textures), avatar bases (meshes), rig types (rig), signed communication (gestures), and moderation features (colliders, stations). Vulnerable demographics could easily be targeted through a world's ability to strip avatars such as furrys, LGBTQ, racial minorities, deaf people, mute people, people with disabilities, etc. This ability could also allow world creators to target other innocent demographics such as non-humanoid avatars, dancers or performers, or quest users.",
